    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20978" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hortānum</span></b> , i,
		n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				city of Etruria</i> (probably called after the Etruscan goddess
			Horta, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. 4, 8</span></i>; cf. Müll. Etrusk.
			II. p. 62), now <i>Orte</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5,
				8, § 52</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hortīnus</span></b> , a, um, <i>of Hortanum</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">classes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 7, 716</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
